## Summary

The working tree already contained the prior attempt's fix; I verified it against every review point and the deterministic-check requirement, made no redundant changes, and confirmed it compiles, lints, and passes the full test suite.

### Final change set (vs `origin/develop`)

**`src/services/contentstack.ts`** — Added the `live_preview` block to the Stack `options` config, gated on `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLED === "true"`, reading `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST` and `CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` (both added to the destructured env vars). No type cast is needed — the installed `contentstack` SDK's `Config` interface natively declares `live_preview?: LivePreview` (host/management_token/enable), so this resolves reviewer advisory #2 cleanly.

**`src/pages/_app.tsx`** — On client mount (`useEffect`, guarded by the preview-enabled flag), calls `ContentstackLivePreview.init({ stackSdk: Stack, clientUrlParams: { host } })` and registers `onEntryChange(() => setLivePreviewKey(k => k + 1))`. The bumped counter is appended to the `<Component key>`, forcing a remount of the page subtree. This keeps both SDK lifecycle calls (`init` + `onEntryChange`) in one place, resolving the minor advisory.

**`src/context/contentstackContext.tsx`, `src/hooks/useContent.ts`, `src/pages/404.tsx`, `src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx`** — Reverted to their original form. Both **blockers** are resolved: the `livePreviewHash`/`isLivePreviewEnabled` fields and the context-threading are gone; the key-remount in `_app.tsx` alone drives re-renders through the existing `ContentstackContext.Provider`/`useContent`/`getContentByKey` pipeline (73 consumers) with zero changes to those files.

**`package.json`** — Removed the bogus direct `lodash-es@4.18.1` dependency and corrected the `lodash` override to the real `4.17.21` (advisory #1). `lodash-es` remains only as a transitive dep of the SDK.

**`.env.local.sample` / `.env.local`** — Document `CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN`, `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST`, and `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLED`.

### Reviewer advisories verified
- **`stackSdk` param (advisory #3):** Confirmed correct. The installed `@contentstack/live-preview-utils@4.4.5` `IInitData` type declares `stackSdk: IStackSdk` and `clientUrlParams` — so `stackSdk` (not the plan's `stack`) is right for this version.

### Helper-usage (deterministic check)
The fix reuses — not re-implements — the existing pipeline: `ContentstackLivePreview.init` wraps the exported `Stack`; `onEntryChange` triggers a remount that re-renders the existing `ContentstackContext.Provider` (in `[[...slug]].tsx`/`404.tsx`), and all consumers read draft content via the unmodified `useContent`/`getContentByKey`. No parallel rendering logic was introduced.

### Verification
- `tsc --noEmit`: clean
- ESLint on changed files: 0 errors (only pre-existing `no-explicit-any` warnings in untouched code)
- Full Jest suite: **247 suites / 1200 tests / 12 snapshots — all passing**

### On the uncovered verification criteria
Four criteria (full published-content render, layout completeness, env-var-driven page load, auth-gated preview) are not covered by automated tests. These are browser/integration-level behaviors — they require the real Contentstack preview service, a running Next.js server, and an authenticated session — and are not exercisable in the Jest/jsdom environment. Test authorship for what *is* unit-testable belongs to the dedicated test-writer agent, per the turn rules.
